Junior Security Analyst, also called a SOC Level 1 Analyst, 
-Security Operations Center (SOC) is a team of IT security professionals tasked with monitoring, preventing, detecting, investigating, and responding to threats within a company’s network and systems.
-work in a 24/7 SOC team
-During your work shift, you would typically:
Monitor and investigate various security alerts
Participate in SOC brainstorms and workshops
Cooperate with other teams to keep your company safe
Constantly learn and discover new attacks and defenses

Which team do you work with as a Junior Security Analyst? -> SOC

==
Senior Analyst - closest colleague. helps you and other Junior analysts when something is unclear and handles complex cases after you do the initial analysis.
SOC Engineer - doesn't have shifts and doesn't analyze the alerts. Instead, he maintains security tools and configures the alerts to make your analyst's job easier.
SOC Manager - tries to keep everything under control. reports SOC results to the top management and makes sure you aren't lost in that big new cyber security world.
Incident Responder - You don't work with Daniel every day, but when he's online, you know something serious has happened. He is called on demand during major incidents.


